{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Matrix Factorization Recommendation.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Matrix Factorization Recommendation.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"matrix factorization recommendation matrix factorization recommendation","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Matrix Factorization Recommendation.md","fileName":"Matrix Factorization Recommendation.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Matrix Factorization Recommendation","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-08 21:16\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[ML.NET Recommendation Applications]] · [[Recommender System Evolution]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["ML.NET Recommendation Applications","Recommender System Evolution","Latent Factor Model","Alternating Least Squares","c80andnetcore30moderncross-platformdevelopment.pdf","frontiersofdatascience.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Matrix Factorization Recommendation.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Matrix Factorization Recommendation.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"matrix factorization recommendation matrix factorization recommendation","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Matrix Factorization Recommendation.md","fileName":"Matrix Factorization Recommendation.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Matrix Factorization Recommendation","heading":"Matrix Factorization Recommendation","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Matrix factorization learns lower-dimensional representations of two kinds of related entities, such as customers and products, from observed interactions. Their learned factors are combined to score pairs that were not directly observed.\n\nIn a co-purchase recommender, transaction relationships provide the training signal and candidate items are ranked by predicted score. The score orders recommendations but should not automatically be interpreted as a calibrated probability of purchase.\n\nAt large scale, matrix factorization summarizes a sparse user-item matrix with [[Latent Factor Model]] representations. [[Alternating Least Squares]] can fit those factors by switching between user and item updates, a structure that supports parallel execution.","tags":["baby"],"links":["ML.NET Recommendation Applications","Recommender System Evolution","Latent Factor Model","Alternating Least Squares","c80andnetcore30moderncross-platformdevelopment.pdf","frontiersofdatascience.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Matrix Factorization Recommendation.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Matrix Factorization Recommendation.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"matrix factorization recommendation matrix factorization recommendation","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Matrix Factorization Recommendation.md","fileName":"Matrix Factorization Recommendation.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Matrix Factorization Recommendation","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[c80andnetcore30moderncross-platformdevelopment.pdf]]\n\n[[frontiersofdatascience.pdf]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["ML.NET Recommendation Applications","Recommender System Evolution","Latent Factor Model","Alternating Least Squares","c80andnetcore30moderncross-platformdevelopment.pdf","frontiersofdatascience.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}